#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <markdown.h>

/**
 * Converts markdown text to HTML.
 *
 * @param markdownText The markdown text to convert.
 * @return The HTML text.
 */
std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdownText) {
    markdown::MarkdownIn markdown(markdownText);
    markdown::MarkdownOut htmlOut;

    markdown.markdown(&markdownIn, &htmlOut);

    return htmlOut.c_str();
}

int main() {
    std::string markdownText = "# Hello, World!";
    std::string htmlText = markdownToHtml(markdownText);

    std::cout << "Markdown: " << markdownText << std::endl;
    std::cout << "HTML: " << htmlText << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

This function uses the markdown library to convert markdown text to HTML. The `markdown::MarkdownIn` object is used to parse the markdown text, and the `markdown::MarkdownOut` object is used to generate the HTML text. The `markdown.markdown` function is used to perform the conversion.

Please note that you need to install the markdown library to use this function. You can install it using your package manager or by downloading it from the official website.

Also, this function assumes that the markdown text is well-formed and does not contain any invalid markdown syntax. If you need to handle invalid markdown syntax, you may need to add error checking code to the function.

